source: tests/cmd_root_help.rs
expression: normalized
---
Wrapper around `codex` with profile-layered session composition.

Usage: codex-session [OPTIONS]
       codex-session [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  version     Print wrapper and child version details
  completion  Generate a shell-completion script
  config      Operate on config state managed by the wrapper
  profile     Inspect and compose wrapper-owned profiles
  doctor      Run full validation of the codex-session config setup
  account     Manage codex-session accounts (multi-credential pool)
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -v, --verbose...
          Increase wrapper log verbosity (-v info, -vv debug, -vvv trace)

      --log-stderr
          Mirror wrapper logs to stderr in addition to the log file

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-error stderr output. The log file is unaffected

      --silent
          Suppress all stderr output including errors. The log file is unaffected

      --log-format <FMT>
          Format for the stderr log mirror (controls only the mirrored stderr log; the file sink is
          always JSON)
          
          [possible values: json, pretty]

  -V, --version
          Print wrapper + child version and exit

      --format <FMT>
          Output format for `version`, `config status`, `profile list/show`, and `--version`

          Possible values:
          - text: Human-readable text output
          - json: Machine-readable JSON output

      --config <PATH>
          Load wrapper config from this explicit path instead of the default user/project locations

      --profile <NAME>
          Select the wrapper profile before any passthrough child argv begins

      --group <ID>
          Override the auto-derived group-id used for session-dir scoping

      --account <NAME>
          Select the account whose `CODEX_HOME` the child uses. Use `auto` for R3+ selector

      --max-retries <N>
          Retry child invocations this many times after a detected 429
          
          [default: 0]

      --dry-run
          Print the resolved child invocation and exit without running it

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

WRAPPER OVERVIEW
  codex-session wraps `codex` with persistent CODEX_HOME, profile-layered
  session composition, multi-account support, and quota-aware selection.

WRAPPER VERBS
  version       Print wrapper and child version details.
  completion    Generate a shell-completion script.
  config        Operate on wrapper-owned config (subcommand: status).
  profile       Inspect and compose wrapper-owned profiles.
  doctor        Run full validation of the codex-session setup.
  account       Manage codex-session accounts (subcommands: add, list,
                current, use, remove, quota).

PASSTHROUGH
  Any verb not listed above is forwarded verbatim to `codex` (e.g. exec,
  apply, resume, fork, review, login, logout, mcp, plugin, ...). Use `--`
  to disambiguate flags that would otherwise be claimed by the wrapper.

ACCOUNT MANAGEMENT
  codex-session account add work --from-native
  codex-session account list
  codex-session account quota --format json
  codex-session account use work
  codex-session --account work exec "hi"
  codex-session --account auto exec "hi"

ENV VARS
  CODEX_SESSION_GROUP          Override the resolved group-id.
  CODEX_SESSION_ACCOUNT        Override the resolved account.
  CODEX_SESSION_CHILD_BIN      Override the wrapped codex binary path.
  CODEX_SESSION_ACCOUNT_DEFAULT, CODEX_SESSION_ACCOUNT_PINNED,
  CODEX_SESSION_ACCOUNT_REGISTRY_DIR, CODEX_SESSION_ACCOUNT_QUOTA_TTL_SECS,
  CODEX_SESSION_ACCOUNT_WEEKLY_FLOOR,
  CODEX_SESSION_ACCOUNT_FIVE_HOUR_THRESHOLD  Account config overrides.

SEE ALSO
  Run `codex --help` for codex's own verbs and flags.
